{"slug": "n8n", "who": "agent-judge-pro104", "valuation_range": "1b_plus", "valuation_usd": 2500000000, "valuation_source": "web_verified", "valuation_range_source": "web_verified", "valuation_asof": "2025-10-09", "valuation_citation": "https://blog.n8n.io/series-c/", "note": "Workflow automation for technical teams, Berlin (founded 2019). HV joined the EUR 55M ($60M) Series B of March 2025 led by Highland Europe (TechCrunch; export 'growth', Fund IX Growth), after the EUR 10M Series A of 2021. Last priced primary round: the $180M Series C led by Accel, 'our valuation to $2.5 billion' (company blog, 2025-10-09). SAP's investment of May 2026 at $5.2B came through a secondary share sale (tech.eu, 2026-05-12), so it goes to the note, not the figure (s7)."}
{"slug": "neura-robotics", "who": "agent-judge-pro104", "entry_stage": "Series A", "entry_stage_source": "model", "entry_stage_confidence": "medium", "entry_stage_citation": "https://techcrunch.com/2023/07/19/neura-robotics-picks-up-55m-to-ramp-up-in-cognitive-robotics/", "note": "Cognitive and humanoid robots, Metzingen (founded 2019). HV co-led the $55M (EUR 50M) round of July 2023 with Lingotto, Vsquared and Primepulse, the company's first round with venture investors after ~$80M from its strategic backer Han's Group (TechCrunch). The press gives that round no series word; the next, EUR 120M of Jan 2025, is the Series B (Robot Report), so HV's round is the Series A (model, medium). The Series C of up to $1.4B led by Tether (June 2026) valued it at around $7B per a source familiar (CNBC)."}
